findings.claim:
Coordinator item (d), extended and measured, with a verdict and a tested fix. The name targets are 19 px tall wherever a name takes one line:
- 'Tropos in Acid' from 430;
- 'Core in Ember' from 432;
- 'Mantle in Ember' from 449;
- 'Hemisphere in Ember' from 492.

Wrapped names are 36 px (two lines) or 53 px (three lines). The pitch is 17 px plus 1 px padding at every square 320-519. OLD's boxes were 37/58/79 px, and 44 px at 505-519. C6e.1's were 37 (58 for a wrapped Tropos).

Against WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 with the real geometry, NEW fails both the 24 px minimum and the spacing exception at 352-374, 388-393 and 407-519 (151 squares). OLD passes at every square 320-519.

The lane's framing ('tap boxes 19 px at 338-386') is the wrong way round. At 338-386 the names wrap, so their boxes are 36-53 px. The 19 px boxes are at 430-519, where the names fit easily.

Verdict: a real regression in conformance and in touch accuracy, but at windows almost no visitor has, so should-fix, not blocking. The names can have 37-44 px targets with all four whole from 463 (tested; CSS below).

C6g-3's 'a name wraps only when wider than the picture' is not met. The small-square row keeps 'padding: 0 10px', so a name wraps as soon as it is within 20 px of the picture's width:
- 'Tropos in Acid' at 405-429;
- 'Core in Ember' at 407-431;
- 'Mantle in Ember' at 424-448;
- 'Hemisphere in Ember' at 467-491.

Each of these names is narrower than the picture there.

The extra line is why 'Tropos in Acid' is clipped at the picture's top until 429: it is 0-52% visible at 405-429 and whole only from 430. A single word wider than the padded row starts 10 px in and overflows to the right, so it is sliced at the picture's right edge:
- 'Mantle' and 'Ember' at 320-358 (350x350 reads 'Mantl / in / Embe', cut by 7.5 px);
- 'Hemisphere' at 389-401 (cut by 10.3 px at 389).

The clip was widened from -2 px to -4 px, so up to 4 px of those letters show past the picture as grey shadow on the page (OLD: 2 px, only at 320-343).

The lane's report says 'at 338-386 names wrap whole instead of being sliced at the sides' and gives Mantle 98% at 350. Both are partly wrong: inside the picture, Mantle is 85% at 350.

items.why:
Line size by square on NEW:
- 17 px at 320-640 (the C6g-7 rule);
- 17 px at 641-960 (the stacked-landscape rule, as C6e.1);
- 14 px at 961-1221, then rising to 16.1 px at 1400, 18 px at 1565 and above (1600x1600 is 18).

Above 640 this is identical to C6e.1 at every square measured. OLD was 17 everywhere.

Correction to coordinator item (h): C6e.1 was 14 px, not 17, at 320-640.

checked:
(c) Non-square windows: NEW is identical to OLD in every measured field at:
- 3,025 grid windows (320-1400 x 300-1400, step 20);
- 1,602 near-squares within 1% (w step 11, every h within 1%);
- 10 portrait monitors (1080x1780, 600x1200, 800x1384, 639x1290 and others; text at x 16 on both);
- 113 real windows.

The only flagged field was the picture file chosen while resizing in place (20 windows). Fresh loads pick the same file on both builds (9 of 9). The only behaviour difference is HR-free and positive: no 84 px bottom scroll padding on the home page.

C6f hero fixes still hold on NEW:
- one left edge at 16 or more at every square (minimum 16, spread 0);
- headline on one line and never cut (at least 54 px inside the window);
- line and both buttons whole on the first screen at all 1,081 squares;
- no sideways scroll;
- portrait monitors at 16 (C6f-6);
- the picture is unchanged from OLD at every window.

Hero names at every square on NEW:
- no name under the sticky header;
- no seen name whose tap centre hits anything but itself;
- real touchscreen taps on the four names open /tropos/acid, /hemisphere/ember, /core/ember and /mantle/ember at 440, 460 and 512.

missed:
HR-1 EXTENSION. At squares 505-519 with overlay scrollbars, NEW does more than lay names over the Core and the Mantle: it also brings back the small-square rule's 192 px dark veil. The lower part of the picture is about 50-60% darker than on OLD, which has no veil there.

Mean luminance of text-free strips at 512x512:
- x168-184, y300-320: 36 on NEW, 94 on OLD;
- x330-344, y300-360: 18 on NEW, 48 on OLD;
- the top strip is the same on both (22.5).

NO BLOCKER MISSED IN THE HERO LENS.

The home page's first screen is pixel-identical on NEW and OLD (ImageMagick AE 0 at 3% fuzz, OLD-vs-OLD baseline also 0) at 16 real windows:
- phones and tablets: 390x844, 375x667, 320x568, 430x932, 844x390, 667x375, 768x1024, 1024x768, 820x1180;
- desktops: 1440x900, 1366x768, 1920x1080;
- classic-scrollbar desktops: 1366x768, 1280x1024, 1024x768, 1536x864.

The home page's only fixed or sticky element is the header. So taking the 84 px bottom scroll padding off the home page costs nothing:
- computed 'auto' on / at 390x844 and 460x460 on NEW;
- still 84px on /tropos/acid and /core/ember.

